# Binary128 coefficients and centers; ascending powers, nearest/even rounding.
# Recomputed with Sollya 8.0, prec=512, fpminimax with 113-bit coefficients.
# SIN/COS use odd/even powers on [2^-100, pi/4] / [0, pi/4].
# EXP uses powers 1..20 for expm1(x*log(2)) on [-1/4, 1/4].
# ATAN/ATANH use odd powers 1..17 on [2^-100, 1/64] / [2^-100, 1/128].
# All fits use relative error. Dividing the odd/EXP fits by x gives the
# stored factors evaluated by kernel.rs; no runtime coefficient generation.
# supnorm(p,f,full_domain,relative,1/1024) certified these conservative
# bounds for the rounded polynomials evaluated in exact real arithmetic:
# SIN < 2^-124, COS < 2^-131, EXP < 2^-116,
# ATAN < 2^-129, ATANH < 2^-135.
# These bounds exclude argument reduction and floating-point evaluation.
# Centers: round(atan(k/32),113,RN) and round(log2(1+k/32),113,RN), k=0..32.
# INV_LN2: round(1/log(2),113,RN).
# Method documentation: https://www.sollya.org/sollya-8.0/help.php?name=fpminimax
# Error certification: https://www.sollya.org/sollya-8.0/help.php?name=supnorm

